One widely adopted strategy is slow steaming, where vessels operate at reduced speeds to lower fuel consumption.
While this method significantly reduces emissions and operational costs, it also leads to longer transit times and potential disruptions in supply chains.
Shipping companies must balance sustainability goals with customer expectations and delivery schedules.
Additionally, regulatory frameworks such as the IMO’s carbon intensity indicators are pushing operators to adopt greener practices, further reinforcing the importance of operational efficiency and environmental responsibility.');
