Ships must follow Traffic Separation Schemes (TSS) to reduce the risk of collision.
Communication between vessels and Vessel Traffic Services (VTS) plays a crucial role in ensuring safe navigation.
Instructions such as reducing speed, altering course, or maintaining safe distance are commonly issued when vessels are in close proximity or crossing paths.
Failure to comply with such instructions can result in dangerous situations, particularly in restricted waters where maneuverability is limited.');
